{
  "configuration_id": "config_037",
  "reason": "The current best is config_039 (multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted) at 0.7250 accuracy. Evidence shows scvi_n200 > pca_n2000 > scgpt for RNA, imagenet_vit_l > resnet50 for image, weighted > concat for fusion, and multiprofile >> single profile. The only untested single-variable perturbation from config_039 that retains all other optimal components is config_037, which swaps transformer aggregation for avgpool. In the RNA-only multiprofile setting, the transformer-avgpool gap was minimal (0.6530 vs 0.6501), and we have no direct evidence of which aggregation is superior in the multimodal+imagenet_vit_l context. This experiment isolates the aggregation effect under the strongest image encoder, providing the highest expected accuracy among remaining options (only a ~0.003 expected drop) and confirming whether transformer aggregation's marginal benefit persists in the multimodal regime. As the final experiment, it maximizes the small probability of matching or exceeding 0.7250 while yielding a clean ablation of aggregation in the best-performing configuration."
}

